      <description>&lt;table cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align: middle; padding-right: 12px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/342800?s=96&amp;amp;v=4&quot; width=&quot;96&quot; height=&quot;96&quot; alt=&quot;@tamirdresher&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0; padding: 0; border-radius: 50%;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher&quot;&gt;Tamir Dresher&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #57606a;&quot;&gt;@tamirdresher&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;Principal Software Engineer @ Microsoft Azure Serverless | Durable Functions | Distributed Systems | AI &amp;amp; Cloud Infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;123&lt;/strong&gt; followers · &lt;strong&gt;3&lt;/strong&gt; following&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;list-style-type: none; padding-left: 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/building.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;building&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;Microsoft&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/map-pin.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;map-pin&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;Israel&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;list-style-type: none; margin-bottom: 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/twitter.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;twitter&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/tamir_dresher&quot;&gt;@tamir_dresher&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Popular Repository&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/squad-skills&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;squad-skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;44 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;9&lt;br&gt;🧩 Reusable skills for GitHub Copilot Squad — Teams automation, podcast generation, and more&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Other Repositories (Popular)&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/RxInAction&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RxInAction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;160 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;57&lt;br&gt;This respository includes the source code for the Reactive Extensions in Action book&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/cli-tunnel&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cli-tunnel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;29 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3&lt;br&gt;Tunnel any CLI app to your phone — PTY + devtunnel + xterm.js&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/holocaust-research-squad-template&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;holocaust-research-squad-template&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;15 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;4&lt;br&gt;A squad of AI researchers for Holocaust family genealogy research. Fork this template and customize for your own family research.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/squad-personal-demo&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;squad-personal-demo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;15 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1&lt;br&gt;My personal AI Squad setup — ralph-watch loop, squad-monitor, Outlook COM automation, podcaster, and more. Companion repo for the blog series.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/WPFLiteTreeView&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WPFLiteTreeView&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;13 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;3&lt;br&gt;WPF Tree View doesn&amp;#39;t scale very good, when you expand a tree item with thousands of items the performance is bad. This TreeView implementation uses a ListBox to simulate a tree&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tamirdresher/squad-on-aks&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;squad-on-aks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;11 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;0&lt;br&gt;🚀 Deploy autonomous AI agent squads on AKS and Azure Container Apps — free tier first, scale later&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Hi there 👋, my name is Tamir Dresher&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;Principal Software Engineer focused on Azure Serverless, Durable Functions, and distributed systems&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://lrqxxq.am.files.1drv.com/y4mXVvaQphG-1hgJK_-PZztvUHGK-10qyOp2wqs2bK-XdtmBi7YvdXg_g2aXefy4TGIIncZxEMkHWStKXbHrEPGlWWBZcendSfsAY1-A0Oth6B3a6KNsOTuN0DLbJuXCq6KcDAIwgPpPr8d7YrZenspZt-R939Ku_NTG92b9o0XmjtVtV_YEG_KhjmS5ha3l3tDPW_cJ0Tvz9bzCjWlERzYLA?width=1182&amp;amp;height=354&amp;amp;cropmode=none&quot; alt=&quot;A software architect passionate about scaling distributed systems and making them reactive &quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am a Principal Software Engineer at Microsoft, working on Azure Serverless platforms with a focus on Durable Functions, workflow orchestration, and large-scale distributed systems. I was previously the President of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.israelclouds.com/iasaisrael&quot;&gt;Israeli Chapter of IASA Global&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br /&gt;Teaching is a big part of my life and since 2013 i&#39;m teaching software engineering at the Ruppin Academic Center &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ruppin.ac.il&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://www.ruppin.ac.il/style%20library/ruppin/Images/logo_en.png&quot; height=&quot;45&quot; style=&quot;vertical-align:middle&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I love writing code and a big fan of .NET (Framework and Core)&lt;/p&gt; 
